{"id":"chebyshev","title":"Chebyshev distance","family":"lock-step","definition":"reference","intro_en":"Chebyshev distance keeps only the largest aligned absolute error. A running maximum identifies the worst discrepancy as the animation scans the sequence. It answers a maximum-deviation question, so a small improvement at the worst point matters while changes below the current maximum may leave the result unchanged.","intro_zh":"Chebyshev 距离只保留最大的逐点绝对误差。动图扫描序列并更新当前最大值，回答最坏偏差有多大的问题。因此最大误差位置的变化很重要，其他位置的小幅变化可能完全不改变结果。","steps_en":["Keep the two series on the same sample grid; no shift or warping is estimated.","Measure the absolute residual; the highlighted point supplies one coordinate contribution.","Update the running maximum.","Keep the largest coordinate discrepancy."],"steps_zh":["在同一采样网格上比较两条序列，不估计平移或时间规整。","计算各坐标的绝对残差。","更新当前最大误差。","以所有坐标中的最大绝对差作为结果。"],"formula":"max_i abs(x_i-y_i)","caveats_en":["One isolated spike may determine the entire result.","Sample alignment and amplitude units are part of the comparison protocol."],"caveats_zh":["一个孤立尖峰就可能决定全部结果。","采样对齐和幅值单位属于比较协议的一部分。"],"sources":[{"label":"SciPy: chebyshev","url":"https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.spatial.distance.chebyshev.html"}],"x":[1.0,1.5,2.4,3.7,4.5,3.8,2.6,2.1,2.8,3.8,4.1,3.3],"y":[1.3,1.8,2.0,3.2,5.2,4.4,2.9,1.6,2.6,3.1,4.4,3.9],"input_label":"Deterministic synthetic illustration; sample index is the time axis.","parameters":{"samples":12,"preprocessing":"none","domain":"strictly positive illustration"},"result":{"label":"distance","value":0.7000000000000002,"detail":"Exact formula evaluation on the displayed aligned vectors."},"frames":[{"phase":0,"caption":"Aligned samples","panel":{"kind":"lines","title":"Aligned samples","a":[1.0,1.5],"a_label":"x","b":[1.3,1.8],"b_label":"y","marker":1}},{"phase":0,"caption":"Aligned samples","panel":{"kind":"lines","title":"Aligned samples","a":[1.0,1.5,2.4,3.7,4.5],"a_label":"x","b":[1.3,1.8,2.0,3.2,5.2],"b_label":"y","mark